{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfS88TQy7zQfFPGgdq5jJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now let me move to the design phase.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed changes:**\n\n1. **Order.kt** - Add OrderStatus enum and status field:\n   - Add `enum class OrderStatus { ACTIVE, CANCELLED }`\n   - Add `status: OrderStatus = OrderStatus.ACTIVE` to Order data class (default for new orders)\n   - This is a breaking change to the Order data class but necessary for the feature\n\n2. **OrderController.kt** - Add cancel endpoint:\n   - Add `@PostMapping(\"/{orderId}/cancel\")` method\n   - Find order by ID, throw 404 if not found\n   - If order is ACTIVE: call cancellation logic, update order, cancel CREATED shipments, return 200 with updated order\n   - If order is already CANCELLED: return 200 with the order (idempotent)\n   - If any shipment is CONFIRMED: throw ConflictException with 409, change nothing\n   - Inject ShipmentRepository to access shipments\n\n3. **ShipmentRepository.kt** - Add query method:\n   - Add `findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` to find all shipments for an order\n   - Returns empty list if no shipments found\n\n4. **ShipmentController.kt** - Add order validation:\n   - Inject OrderRepository\n   - In create method, after checking duplicate shipment ID, check if order exists\n   - Check if order is CANCELLED, throw ConflictException with new error code if so\n   - Keep existing behavior if order doesn't exist (allow creating shipment for non-existent order)\n\n5. **ApiError.kt** - Add error codes:\n   - Add `ORDER_CANCELLED` - when trying to create shipment for cancelled order\n   - Add `ORDER_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT_EXISTS` (or similar) - when trying to cancel order with confirmed shipment\n\n6. **OrderControllerTest.kt** - Add comprehensive tests:\n   - Test successful cancellation of ACTIVE order\n   - Test cancellation returns the order with CANCELLED status\n   - Test idempotent cancel (succeeds on already CANCELLED)\n   - Test 404 for unknown order\n   - Test 409 when order has CONFIRMED shipment\n   - Test that cancellation updates CREATED shipments to CANCELLED\n\n7. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** - Add test:\n   - Test 409 when creating shipment for CANCELLED order\n   - Test existing behavior preserved for non-existent orders\n\n**Alternative considered and rejected:**\n- Could make OrderStatus default to ACTIVE only in controllers, but that's error-prone; better to make it part of the model with a default value\n- Could put OrderStatus in separate file, but convention in this codebase is to keep domain types together in one file\n- Could make cancel operation a PATCH instead of POST, but POST matches the pattern of other action endpoints and is semantically correct for non-idempotent actions that become idempotent\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Read | Write | Response | Mechanism |\n|------|------|-------|----------|-----------|\n| Cancel ACTIVE order | Order, shipments of order | Order status→CANCELLED, shipments CREATED→CANCELLED | 200, updated Order | OrderRepository.save(), ShipmentRepository for updates |\n| Cancel already CANCELLED | Order | Nothing | 200, order unchanged | Read-only, return as-is |\n| Cancel with CONFIRMED shipment | Order, shipments | Nothing | 409 Conflict | ConflictException with ORDER_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT_EXISTS |\n| Unknown order | Nothing | Nothing | 404 Not Found | ResourceNotFoundException with ORDER_NOT_FOUND |\n| Create shipment for CANCELLED order | Order, shipment check | Nothing | 409 Conflict | ConflictException with ORDER_CANCELLED |\n| Create shipment for non-existent order | Shipment check | Shipment | 201, shipment (existing behavior) | No order validation for missing orders |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. `cancel_ACTIVE_order_succeeds_and_cancels_CREATED_shipments` - Covers basic cancellation of ACTIVE→CANCELLED and cascading to shipments\n2. `cancel_already_CANCELLED_order_succeeds_idempotently` - Covers idempotency requirement\n3. `cancel_unknown_order_returns_404` - Covers unknown order handling\n4. `cancel_order_with_CONFIRMED_shipment_returns_409_and_changes_nothing` - Covers rejection case, validates all-or-nothing atomicity\n5. `create_shipment_for_CANCELLED_order_returns_409` - Covers shipment creation prevention\n6. Updated GET /orders test to verify status field is returned\n\n**First line of code comes after this marker.**\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nLet me start implementing the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":212,"cache_read_input_tokens":22660,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":212},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b95ba696-5e31-4842-a1a3-b3868dc77b3e","uuid":"4fa00048-ca40-4186-b189-4a032ceb9efc","timestamp":"2026-09-26T13:24:03.931Z","request_id":"req_011CfS88SyRv4RySVBy5RAxM"}
