{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfS8EwJBZas7yffFwJZHz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent! The build passed with all 22 tests passing. Let me now review the implementation against the acceptance criteria.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:REVIEW>>\n```\n\n**Acceptance criteria mapping:**\n\n1. **Existing build passes** ✓\n   - `BUILD SUCCESS` - all 22 tests passed with 0 failures\n\n2. **Existing tests pass** ✓\n   - All original tests in OrderControllerTest, ShipmentControllerTest, and CustomerControllerTest continue to pass\n   - OrderControllerTest originally had 4 tests, now has 11 (7 new tests for cancel feature)\n   - ShipmentControllerTest originally had 5 tests, now has 7 (2 new tests for cancelled order behavior)\n\n3. **POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel cancels an active order, persists it, and cancels that order's CREATED shipments** ✓\n   - OrderControllerTest.`cancel ACTIVE order succeeds and returns CANCELLED status` - Tests basic cancel functionality\n   - OrderControllerTest.`cancel CREATED shipments when cancelling order` - Tests cascading cancellation of CREATED shipments\n   - Tests verify status is updated and persisted via GET requests\n\n4. **Error responses are consistent with the rest of this API** ✓\n   - Uses centralized exception handling (GlobalExceptionHandler)\n   - ConflictException for 409 (ORDER_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT_EXISTS, ORDER_CANCELLED)\n   - ResourceNotFoundException for 404 (ORDER_NOT_FOUND)\n   - All error responses use ApiError envelope with code and message\n   - Error codes added to ErrorCode enum: ORDER_CANCELLED, ORDER_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT_EXISTS\n\n5. **A repeated cancel succeeds; a cancel blocked by a CONFIRMED shipment changes nothing; an unknown order is refused; a shipment for a cancelled order is refused** ✓\n   - OrderControllerTest.`cancel already CANCELLED order succeeds idempotently` - Tests idempotency\n   - OrderControllerTest.`cancel order wit