e for rejected order cancellation\n   - Both are necessary for proper error signaling\n\n6. **OrderControllerTest.kt** - Required change:\n   - Added 7 new tests covering all cancel endpoint scenarios\n   - Also updated @BeforeEach to clear shipment repository\n\n7. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** - Required change:\n   - Added 2 new tests for cancelled order behavior\n   - Updated @BeforeEach to clear order repository\n\n**Unresolved findings:**\n\nNone. All ticket requirements have been implemented and tested.\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DONE>>\n```\n\nRequirement: Add POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel endpoint to cancel orders with status tracking, cascading shipment cancellation, idempotency, and conflict detection.\n\nChanged:\n- Order.kt: Added OrderStatus enum and status field to Order data class\n- OrderController.kt: Added /cancel endpoint with full cancellation logic\n- ShipmentRepository.kt: Added findByOrderId method for querying shipments\n- ShipmentController.kt: Added order validation to prevent shipment creation on cancelled orders\n- ApiError.kt: Added ORDER_CANCELLED and ORDER_CONFIRMED_SHIPMENT_EXISTS error codes\n- OrderControllerTest.kt: Added 7 tests for cancel functionality, updated setUp\n- ShipmentControllerTest.kt: Added 2 tests for cancelled order behavior, updated setUp\n\nTests:\n- test_cancel_ACTIVE_order_succeeds_and_returns_CANCELLED_status: Verifies basic cancellation updates order status\n- test_cancel_already_CANCELLED_order_succeeds_idempotently: Verifies idempotent behavior\n- test_cancel_unknown_order_returns_404: Verifies 404 for non-existent orders\n- test_cancel_CREATED_shipments_when_cancelling_order: Verifies cascading shipment cancellation\n- test_cancel_order_with_CONFIRMED_shipment_returns_409_and_changes_nothing: Verifies all-or-nothing rejection\n- test_new_order_starts_in_ACTIVE_status: Verifies orders default to ACTIVE\n- test_cancel_order_does_not_affect_CANCELLED_shipments: Verifies only CREATED shipments are cancelled\n- test_rejec